  MRNA [neutral]: Moderna began a landmark early-stage trial in Uganda of its experimental Ebola vaccine, the first evaluation in children from age 1. Stocktwits reports MRNA is on track for a fourth straight monthly gain, and Simply Wall St cites significant insider selling over the past three months. Invesco S&P 500 Equal Weight (RSP) reported buying $2.7 million more Moderna on Nov. 25.
  SNDK [positive]: SanDisk (SNDK) shares rose roughly 13% to 16% on November 27, 2026, as memory stocks rebounded after losing nearly half their value over the prior month. The move followed a Kioxia and Nvidia proof of concept that used 144 Kioxia SSDs in an Nvidia GB200 rack to reach about 1.1 petabytes of extended memory. Broader U.S. indexes also rose in the post-Thanksgiving session.
  MU [neutral]: Micron (MU) shares rose 4.29% on November 27, 2026, in a broader chip-sector rebound after a volatile stretch in which the Nasdaq-100 briefly fell about 20% below its October 6 record close. Headlines cite 26 take-or-pay customer deals worth $32 billion in cash and commitments, and a CEO view that memory shortages could worsen in 2028, while TrendForce expects memory prices to start falling in early 2028.
  DELL [positive]: Dell Technologies stock rose after strong fiscal Q3 results, with revenue doubling to $54.9 billion and a raised fiscal 2027 outlook of $202 billion alongside a new $25 billion buyback. The company cited a $132.3 billion AI backlog, while UBS said the results did not ease concerns about the durability of AI spending. Reports also flagged new U.S. semiconductor export controls on Nvidia chips in Asia as a regulatory uncertainty for AI server makers like Dell.
  LITE [neutral]: Lumentum (LITE) rose along with other optical stocks after a broad AI-related selloff on Wednesday, with Applied Optoelectronics and Lumentum up 7% in a rebound. Coverage notes the stock is up about 55% over the past year on AI-driven optical networking demand, while also citing rising costs, a premium valuation, and uncertainty tied to an acquisition, including a reference to a $115 billion all-stock bet on Lumentum by Marvell.
  SPCX [positive]: SpaceX (SPCX) shares rose on November 27, 2026, after the FCC approved the Starmind plan for one million AI satellites, which opens a regulatory path to orbital data centers with a first launch targeted for Q3 2027. Shares also climbed after Elon Musk expanded his pledge to give two shares to each American child with an active Trump Account. A Yahoo Finance report noted the stock was still trading below its $135 IPO price.
  PLTR [positive]: Palantir shares rose about 3.72% after reports of a five-year, roughly $300 million software contract with Poland's defense ministry, which would give Poland's armed forces access to Palantir's Maven Smart System. Other coverage noted the company's raised 2026 growth outlook of 91% and a $122M sale of PLTR shares by Peter Thiel.

